    19	        ...
    20	
    21	## Design principles
    22	
    23	1. **stdlib only** — Python >= 3.9, no external deps.
    24	2. **Fail-safe** — a git command failure does not crash the walker;
    25	   the caller handles empty iteration.
    26	3. **Unified allowlist** — three styles of allowlist entry (exact
    27	   path, glob pattern, substring token) can be mixed. `is_allowlisted`
    28	   returns True if ANY style matches.
    29	4. **Mode-specific collection, mode-agnostic filtering** — the walker
    30	   gathers candidate paths differently in git vs filesystem mode, but
    31	   applies the same filtering pipeline.
    32	
    33	## Modes
    34	
    35	- `"filesystem"` — uses `Path.rglob()` starting from `repo_root`.
    36	  Respects `suffixes` and `skip_subdir_names`. Used by tier-boundaries.
    37	- `"git"` — runs `git ls-files -z` from `repo_root`. Returns all
    38	  tracked files; `.gitignore` is honored by git itself. Used by
    39	  contamination check.
    40	"""
